\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Conjecture}
\title{A plateau for the cycle}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{Let #{Z_N} be the heat trace of the cycle in
\ref{fdip-00CS}. The sequence #{C_N} has a
[plateau](fdip-00CO) at #{1} along some windows
#{0<a_N<b_N} for which #{a_N\to\infty},
#{b_N/N^2\to 0} and #{b_N/a_N\to\infty}. The Cartesian
product of #{d} copies of #{C_N}, for any positive integer
#{d} and with the same windows, then has a
[plateau](fdip-00CO) at #{d}. This follows from
\ref{fdip-00CQ} applied one factor at a time.}
